## Why This Is Asked

Evaluates practical implementation of CKNE-driven throughput control at the API gateway layer, specifically assessing the ability to translate abstract CKNE values into concrete resource quotas and deadlines, and to adapt these allocations in real-time based on performance metrics.

## Key Concepts

- Dynamic CKNE-to-resource quota mapping
- Token bucket algorithm with CKNE-weighted refill rates
- Real-time rebalancing loop with SLA preservation
- Fairness constraints while prioritizing high-value tenants

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudocode: CKNE-driven resource rebalancing executed minute-by-minute
function rebalanceResources(tenants) {
  tenants.forEach(tenant => {
    // Scale token refill rate by CKNE value
    tenant.tokens += baseRefillRate * tenant.ckne;

    // Adjust upstream deadline inversely with CKNE
    tenant.deadline = baseDeadline / (tenant.ckne + 1);

    // Enforce maximum allocation caps
    tenant.tokens = Math.min(tenant.tokens, maxTokenCap);
  });
}
```

## Implementation Strategy

The system continuously monitors per-tenant performance metrics and reallocates resources toward higher-CKNE tenants while maintaining baseline p95 latency guarantees through a controlled feedback loop that preserves fairness across the tenant population.
